hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1787","Ameer-ul-Mu'mineen Sayyiduna Ali bin Abi Talib (may Allah be pleased with him) said that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) sent me, Zubair, and Miqdad (may Allah be pleased with them) to the place of Rawzah Khakh, saying that there is a woman there who has a letter; bring it... Then the entire incident of Hatib bin Balta'ah was narrated, and at the end it was said that at that time this verse was revealed: ""O you who believe! Do not take My enemies and your enemies as friends. You send messages of friendship to them, while they..."" etc."
"1788","Lady Umm ‘Atiyyah (may Allah be pleased with her) said: We pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), and this verse was recited: “That they will not associate anything with Allah.” And he forbade us from wailing (over the dead). Then a woman withdrew her hand from the pledge and said, “So-and-so woman helped me in wailing; should I not repay her?” The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) did not say anything. She went away and (after wailing) came back, and the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) accepted her pledge. (That woman was herself Umm ‘Atiyyah, may Allah be pleased with her.)"
